  <name>SolidCraft</name>
  <summary>Parametric 3D CAD in the style of Fusion</summary>
  <metadata_license>CC0-1.0</metadata_license>
  <project_license>MIT OR Apache-2.0</project_license>
  <developer id="io.github.bherbruck">
    <name>SolidCraft contributors</name>
  </developer>
  <url type="homepage">https://solidcraft.io</url>
  <url type="bugtracker">https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft/issues</url>
  <url type="vcs-browser">https://github.com/tangency-labs/solidcraft</url>
  <description>
    <p>This is a community package of SolidCraft, maintained independently and unaffiliated with the SolidCraft project. It repackages the official upstream Linux release build unmodified.</p>
    <p>SolidCraft is an open-source parametric 3D CAD application written in Rust. Sketch on a plane, constrain and dimension the sketch, turn profiles into solids on a feature timeline, and change a parameter to watch the timeline rebuild.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sketches with a constraint solver and parameter-driven dimensions</li>
      <li>Extrude, revolve, sweep, loft, fillet, chamfer, shell, holes and patterns</li>
      <li>Components and joints, sheet metal, and a plastic-enclosure subset</li>
      <li>STEP and IGES import and export; 3MF, STL and OBJ</li>
      <li>Every action is a command, scriptable from a CLI, a JSON control channel and an MCP server</li>
    </ul>
    <p>The headless command runner and MCP server is included: <code>flatpak run --command=solidcraft-cli io.github.bherbruck.SolidCraft --help</code></p>
    <p>Permissions: this package uses the same sandbox as upstream's own Flatpak manifest: display (Wayland, with X11 as a fallback), the GPU device, and the Documents folder. It also grants the spacenavd socket (/run/spnav.sock), so a 3D mouse works when spacenavd is running. Files anywhere else are opened and saved through the system file chooser. No network access is granted.</p>
    <p>Optional overrides:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Let agents on the host reach the <code>--control</code> automation server: <code>flatpak override --user --share=network io.github.bherbruck.SolidCraft</code></li>
      <li>Open files by path anywhere in your home folder: <code>flatpak override --user --filesystem=home io.github.bherbruck.SolidCraft</code></li>
    </ul>
  </description>
